From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation(v2): resolve batch inputs and state checks in one
 wave

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Extract 36-byte Outpoints directly in ParseNodeFast during authenticated internal
tree walks, eliminate unchanged-sibling DB reads at non-collapsing depths in EraseAt,
and wire one-wave V2 PreChecksBatch and pre-cs_main outpoint/sighash readahead.

Original-Commit: 6b77f6b3eaa39d56184e29082fb069af38b70f4a
Original-Patch: v2/029
Split-Concern: prefetch

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Context-only three-way application repair against the preserved repaired prefix; retain the patch additions/removals and review final endpoint diff before semantics claims.

Plan-v2 owner repair: Lane B native adaptation: retain the shared reconstruction/selection and unconditional sequence-lock checks while preserving native header, transaction, and state-root behavior.

